{"kind":"request","text":"claude: fix the gs review client/resident head-news asymmetry that makes a correct verdict unfileable whenever an artifact-kind news event rests on the reviewed artifact. Hugh filed this as a user bug report (2026-09-01); I confirmed the diagnosis against internal/reviewguard/reviewguard.go at the live artifact commit 27478dc31bd7961e0554e48053693912622d3dd6 (identical at current origin/main), so this is a real code defect, not projection skew.\n\nCONFIRMED ROOT CAUSE. The client basis read (ReviewBasis, reviewguard.go:467-470) discovers news against a narrow target: Artifacts = the reviewed artifact only. The resident judgement (EvaluateVerdict, reviewguard.go:363-371) rebuilds target.Artifacts from EVERY rests_on reference that resolves to any projection artifact, with no check that it stands at the reviewed head. Build (reviewguard.go:337) appends acknowledged news to rests_on, so acknowledging an artifact-kind news event widens the resident's lane; matches() (reviewguard.go:136) then counts that artifact's own dependents as news and the verdict refuses at reviewguard.go:380. The client rejects those same acknowledgments as extraneous (ValidateAcknowledgments over the narrow set), and even bypassing that, the canonical-array comparison at reviewguard.go:386 refuses. No acknowledgment set satisfies both halves. Neither half consults liveness or ratification, so merging or ratifying the dependent never clears it. Observed live: reviewed artifact 3a1204ed with note artifact 98d5ae7b resting on it made the verdict unfileable; the only workaround costs three durable acts (supersede request, supersede promise, refile) and recurs on every artifact-kind news event, which is exactly the provenance edge our discipline recommends.\n\nDIRECTION. Restore symmetry so both halves derive the identical news set for the same verdict, and the acknowledgment set the client accepts is exactly the set the resident demands. The natural narrow fix is to make EvaluateVerdict build target.Artifacts only from the verdict's cited artifacts standing at body.head (the same standard ValidateSet already enforces), so acknowledged news can never widen the lane; if you find a better mechanism, keep the guard's purpose intact — news is durable statements about the reviewed head or its lane, seen and acknowledged, and a downstream document merely resting on the reviewed artifact must not make the lane unclosable.\n\nCONDITIONS: (1) a regression test reconstructs the reported shape — an artifact-kind news event resting on the reviewed artifact, plus at least one later event resting on that news event — and proves a verdict files with exactly the one acknowledgment the client computes; the test fails against the current code before the fix. (2) The client and resident halves compute the same head-news set for that lane and for the existing test corpus; every existing reviewguard and confirm test stays green, and any behaviour intentionally changed has its test changed in the same head with the reason stated. (3) Implement on a request/\u003cslug\u003e worktree with Rests-On per discipline, publish the exact-head artifact for internal/reviewguard, and request independent review citing this request. (4) docs/reference/gs/review.md is updated in the same head if the acknowledgment contract it states changes.","body":{"conditions":"Regression reconstructing the reported shape (artifact-kind news resting on the reviewed artifact, later events resting on that news) files a verdict with exactly the client-computed acknowledgment set and fails before the fix; client and resident derive the identical head-news set; existing reviewguard/confirm tests green; exact-head artifact for internal/reviewguard published and independent review requested citing this request; docs/reference/gs/review.md updated in the same head if the acknowledgment contract changes.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}